# .NET backend conventions

> Rationale lives in `docs/architecture/backend-architecture.md`. This file is conventions only.

## Project layout

```
Vni.Ielts.Domain/          entities, value objects, IELTS rules. No dependencies.
Vni.Ielts.Application/     use cases, port interfaces, DTOs.
Vni.Ielts.Infrastructure/  Mongo repos, AI adapters, storage.
Vni.Ielts.Api/             controllers, auth, DI wiring.
Vni.Ielts.Worker/          background job host.
```

Dependencies point **inward only**. `Domain` references nothing.

Organise by **feature** inside each project (`Identity/`, `Exams/`, `Sessions/`, `Evaluation/`, `Cms/`, `Rewards/`) — not by technical type (`Services/`, `Handlers/`, `Interfaces/`).

## The boundary rule

**No `[Bson*]` attributes, `ObjectId`, `BsonDocument`, or any driver type on domain entities.** Persistence models live in `Infrastructure` and map to domain entities.

```csharp
// Domain — clean
public sealed class ExamSession
{
    public ExamSessionId Id { get; private set; }
    public DateTimeOffset DeadlineAt { get; private set; }
    public bool IsWithinDeadline(DateTimeOffset serverNow) => serverNow <= DeadlineAt;
}

// Infrastructure — persistence concerns isolated here
internal sealed class ExamSessionDocument
{
    [BsonId] public ObjectId Id { get; set; }
}
```

## Style

- File-scoped namespaces.
- `sealed` by default on classes not designed for inheritance.
- `record` for DTOs and value objects; `class` for entities with identity.
- Nullable reference types enabled; do not suppress warnings with `!` without a comment explaining why.
- `async`/`await` throughout; always accept and pass `CancellationToken`.
- Never `async void` except for event handlers.
- Prefer `IReadOnlyList<T>` / `IReadOnlyCollection<T>` on public surfaces.

## Types that carry meaning

- **Strongly-typed IDs** (`ExamSessionId`, not `string` or `ObjectId`).
- **`BandScore` value type**, not `double`. Reject invalid values at construction — valid bands are the closed set `0, 0.5, … 9`.
- **`DateTimeOffset` in UTC**, never `DateTime`. Exam deadlines cross timezones.
- **`decimal` for scores and money-like values**, never `float`/`double`.

## Timing

Timing values come from the server clock. **Never accept a client-supplied timestamp** for `startedAt`, `deadlineAt`, or submission time. Reject late submissions with `409 SESSION_EXPIRED`.

## Band rounding

The overall-band rule has asymmetric special cases (`.25` → up to half band, `.75` → up to whole band). **Do not use a generic rounding helper** — it gets `.75` wrong. Give it a dedicated function and a table-driven test.

## Testing

- xUnit. One assert concept per test; name as `Method_Scenario_ExpectedOutcome`.
- Domain: pure unit tests, no I/O.
- Infrastructure: Testcontainers against real MongoDB, not mocks of the driver.
- Architecture tests enforcing dependency direction — these are not optional.
- **Never assert against a live AI provider.** Fixtures only.
